{
  "manufacturer": "Lumel",
  "manufacturer_slug": "lumel",
  "model": "NMID31 / NMID32 three-phase energy meter",
  "model_slug": "nmid32",
  "short_model": "NMID32",
  "aliases": [
    "NMID31",
    "NMID32"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy meter (DIN-rail, three-phase, MID)",
  "applies_to": "Lumel NMID31 and NMID32 DIN-rail single/three-phase energy meters with RS-485 Modbus RTU, per their interface manual.",
  "summary": "DIN-rail MID energy meters for 1- and 3-phase networks with an RS-485 Modbus RTU port. Values are IEEE-754 floats in two registers, high word first by default, readable as input registers (3X) and mirrored in the 4X area. This map covers table 1.1: per-phase and system values, demands, energies, THD and hour counters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Table 1.1 prints Modicon numbers (30001) next to the hex start address (00 00). The hex column is the wire address, so 30001 is register 0."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "NMID32 / NMID31 Digital energy meter - Interface manual",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.lumel.com.pl/resources/Pliki%20do%20pobrania/liczniki%20energii/NMID31_NMID32_interface_manual.pdf",
    "pages": "RS-485 format and example frames pp. 3-5; Table 1.1 pp. 6-8; Table 3 (4X setup incl. word order) pp. 13-15 (PDF pages 7-15)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Floats are IEEE-754, most significant byte first in normal mode; the example frames return 43 5B 41 06 (219.254 V) and 44 FA 00 00 (2000 W), so high word first.",
    "The word order can be reversed by writing 2141.0 to the word-order setup register (Table 3 lists it at 46053, the description text at 46055); this map assumes the normal order.",
    "The same values sit in the 4X area at the same offsets; only the 3X copy is listed.",
    "Left out: 0x32 'Watt Avg' (no unit printed), 0x4E 'VArh export' (unit printed kVAh), 0x5E 'max kVAr Imp. demand' (name says kVAr, unit column says VAr) row 77 'Wh Total Resetable' (hex address misprinted '.98'); the per-phase and tariff energy tables 1.2/1.3 because their Modicon numbers and hex addresses disagree in places; the 32-bit integer energy tables and the 4X setup table."
  ],
